clearcote(#11): Sec-CH-DPR must follow the persona.

window.devicePixelRatio was overridden in the renderer while the Sec-CH-DPR client hint kept
reporting the host's real display, so any site that opted into client hints received both values in
a single page load and could see them disagree -- with no fingerprinting work of its own, and no
population baseline needed. Reported against 149; the sibling Sec-CH-Device-Memory defect was
already fixed by 030, which works precisely because both channels read one blink/common function.

Two producers had to change, which is why the first attempt at this fix failed verification:

  * content/browser/client_hints/client_hints.cc  -- the browser adds the hint on navigation
  * third_party/blink/.../loader/frame_fetch_context.cc -- the renderer adds it for fetches, and
    read Document::DevicePixelRatio(), a DIFFERENT accessor from the LocalDOMWindow getter the
    persona overrides

Both now resolve through ungoogled::PersonaDevicePixelRatio() (flag > persona > none), so the rule
lives in one place and the two channels cannot disagree. The overridden header is deliberately not
zoom-scaled, because the JS value the persona returns does not track zoom either.

Verified on both platforms, host DPR 1, persona DPR forced to 2 and 3: header and JS agree in every
configuration tested.

--- a/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h
+++ b/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.h
@@ -249,6 +249,18 @@
 // persona; later calls return the same one. Thread-safe (std::call_once).
 COMPONENT_EXPORT(UNGOOGLED) const PersonaProfile& CurrentPersona();
 
+// clearcote: the device pixel ratio this persona presents, or 0 when there is no
+// override and the caller should fall back to the real display value. Resolution
+// order is flag > persona > none, which is what window.devicePixelRatio returns.
+//
+// SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH -- both window.devicePixelRatio (renderer) and the
+// Sec-CH-DPR client hint (browser process) must resolve through this. When only
+// the renderer applied the override, a site that opted into client hints got the
+// real display DPR on the wire and the persona value in JS, so the browser
+// contradicted itself inside one page load with no fingerprinting work required
+// of the site. Two code paths must never own the same rule.
+COMPONENT_EXPORT(UNGOOGLED) double PersonaDevicePixelRatio();
+
 // clearcote: the persona's speechSynthesis voice list, retargeted to the
 // persona's locale. |accept_languages| is the RendererPreferences
 // Accept-Language string -- the SAME field blink::Settings::GetAcceptLanguages()
